From ca665d6166f6222fe185e1eac9f2cb358f0624a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] hostgap: host-computed draft kv_indptr for the multi-step
 draft backend

FlashInferMultiStepDraftBackend.common_template copies the per-step
kv_indptr rows to the host with .cpu() after generate_draft_decode_kv_indices
writes them, which blocks until the GPU has finished everything queued
before the draft (the previous draft extend). The kernel's rows are
sum(positions[:z]) + z * (step + 1), with the draft positions equal to each
request's committed length repeated top-k times and zero on CUDA-graph
padding rows, so the host computes them from seq_lens_cpu.

SGLANG_HOSTGAP_DRAFT_INDPTR=1 uses the host rows on replays and eager
draft passes (capture keeps the device read); SGLANG_HOSTGAP_VALIDATE=1
also reads the device rows and raises on any difference. The pinned-buffer
guard from the verify patch covers this flag too. Off by default.
